<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>preview</LangVersion>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsPublishable>false</IsPublishable>
    <RootNamespace>Stomme.Persistence.Conformance.Tests</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    The persistence seam's PROVIDER CONFORMANCE suite: one set of contract tests, run against
    every provider. A test that only one provider passes is a seam that is not a seam.

    GATED: this project IS in Stomme.slnx, so `dotnet test Stomme.slnx` runs it. It needs a live
    RavenDB server via RAVENDB_TEST_URL — the infra UAT tier, http://192.168.10.20:8081 (the old local :7000
    default named here until 2026-08-02 is RETIRED; in CI the ci-db-gated.yml parity-suite job points it at a
    job-local service container instead). When that server is absent the suite FAILS. That is the point: an
    EF-only run of a parity suite certifies nothing, so parity untested reads as failure rather than a green
    skip. RavenParityCoverageTests is the named diagnosis.

    The SQLite EF half needs nothing (in-memory for the Widget half, two connections for the framework-store
    half). Since BL-16 the suite ALSO needs a live PostgreSQL — the Postgres* fixtures run the same contracts
    against a scratch database on the infra UAT tier (POSTGRES_TEST_HOST/PORT/USER/PASSWORD, defaulting to
    192.168.10.20:5433 with DEFAULT_PASSWORD) and FAIL, not skip, when it is unreachable, for the same D46
    reason: a SQLite-only EF half cannot represent PostgreSQL's answers (PostgresParityCoverageTests is the
    named diagnosis).

    Until D46 this project was in no .slnx, on the stated grounds that the Raven half "is skipped when it
    is unreachable". That claim was false — measured at Failed: 48, Passed: 45 with the server down. It
    never skipped; it failed without saying why.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" />
    <PackageReference Include="AwesomeAssertions" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite" />
    <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlite3" />
    <!-- The PostgreSQL fixtures (PostgresConformanceTests / PostgresFrameworkStoreConformanceTests).
         Both EF fixtures above are SQLite, which structurally cannot represent PostgreSQL's answers (its
         LIKE is case-SENSITIVE where SQLite's is not — the D46 ADR's own stated limit), so the suite now
         also runs against a live PG scratch database on the infra tier (POSTGRES_TEST_* / DEFAULT_PASSWORD). -->
    <PackageReference Include="Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL" />
    <!-- D83 security pin: force the patched System.Drawing.Common (central 10.0.10) over the transitive
         4.7.0 pulled through Stomme.Server -> Sustainsys.Saml2 (GHSA-rxg9-xrhp-64gj, CRITICAL, NU1904).
         This is the sole project the sweep surfaces it in; a direct reference is required because central
         transitive pinning is off in this repo. -->
    <PackageReference Include="System.Drawing.Common" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Stomme.Persistence.RavenDb\Stomme.Persistence.RavenDb.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Stomme.Persistence.EfCore\Stomme.Persistence.EfCore.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Stomme.Persistence.Abstractions\Stomme.Persistence.Abstractions.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Stomme.SharedKernel\Stomme.SharedKernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Stomme.Tenancy.Domain\Stomme.Tenancy.Domain.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Stomme.Tenancy.Abstractions\Stomme.Tenancy.Abstractions.csproj" />
    <!-- The FRAMEWORK-STORE half of the suite (FrameworkStoreConformanceTests). The eight closed
         I{Aggregate}Store interfaces and the aggregates they persist are declared in Stomme.Server, so a
         suite that exercises the clusters has to reference it.

         This is what the Widget half deliberately avoids (see the note below) — and the note still holds for
         that half: Widget stays free of Stomme.Shared so the seam's own contract is testable without the
         CMS model surface. The cluster tests cannot make that trade, because the clusters ARE the CMS model.
         Both halves live in one project on purpose: one conformance suite, one command, every provider. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Stomme.Server\Stomme.Server.csproj" />
    <!-- NOTE: the Widget half deliberately does NOT depend on Stomme.Shared for Stomme.Models.IAuditable.
         That project is the CMS model surface and carries the gRPC/protobuf contract build; binding the
         seam's own conformance tests to it would drag protoc codegen into a test about storage. Widget
         mirrors IAuditable's shape instead — which is exactly what AuditStamp matches (see its remarks). -->
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
